@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title POST /api/workspace/v1/messenger/messages/
actor "The client ." as Client
participant "WorkspaceMessageController\nRestAlchemy" as API
database "PostgreSQL\ncanonical lines + brackets" as DB
queue "Transactional outbox\n+ Typed tasks" as Outbox
participant "Background performers\nexact scope leases + fencing" as Worker
database "Ready projections\nThe container is tied up ." as Projection
database "The public events repository" as Events
participant "The controller . WebSocket" as Dispatcher
actor "The client . WebSocket" as WS
Client -> API: POST /api/workspace/v1/messenger/messages/
API -> DB: One transaction: MESSAGE + - That 's it . TOPIC placement(UUIDv5)\n+ The author 's USER_MESSAGE_BINDING + USER_MESSAGE_STATE
API -> DB: immutable outbox event For each typed task
DB --> API: The transaction is recorded
API --> Client: A successful public response
DB ->> Outbox: The events that have been recorded
Outbox ->> Worker: fanout / content_mentions / read_counters /\nfolder_projection / delivery_snapshot_event\neach task It has its own outbox_event_uuid
Worker -> Worker: topic newest-first; recipient batches user_uuid ASC\ndefault 1000, max 5000; bounded fairness
alt Placing the flow with yourself
    Worker -> Projection: No additional USER_MESSAGE_BINDING\nor USER_MESSAGE_STATE; Update the owners projection
else the usual/direct placement
    Worker -> DB: keyset batch; active membership + expected generation
    group One . batch DB transaction
      Worker -> Projection: bulk binding + state + downstream work
      Worker -> Events: durable ready rows + checkpoint / next batch
    end
end
Events ->> Dispatcher: fixed ready line
Dispatcher ->> WS: I 'm going to send / repeat / reproduce
note over API,Projection
  Public uuid = MESSAGE_PLACEMENT.uuid =
  UUIDv5(namespace=TOPIC.uuid, name=MESSAGE.uuid).
  Name — lowercase hyphenated canonical UUID.
  MESSAGE.uuid and binding_uuid They 're hidden ..
  Lease/fencing, retry/backoff, DLQ/reaper - They 're compulsory ..
end note
@enduml
